<concept_spec>

concept SavedProject

purpose
  to allow learners to bookmark/save projects for later viewing

state
  a set of SavedProjects with
    an id String
    a userId String
    a projectId String
    optional notes String
    a createdAt Date
    an updatedAt Date

actions
  save(userId: String, projectId: String, notes: String?) -> SavedProject | {error}
    - create a new saved project bookmark
    - validate userId and projectId exist
    - prevent duplicate saves (same user + project)
    - return saved project with timestamp

  unsave(userId: String, projectId: String) -> {success: Boolean} | {error}
    - remove a saved project bookmark
    - return success status

  updateNotes(userId: String, projectId: String, notes: String) -> SavedProject | {error}
    - update notes for a saved project
    - return updated saved project

queries
  _getByUser(userId: String) -> [SavedProject]
    - return all projects saved by a user
    - ordered by most recently saved

  _getByProject(projectId: String) -> [SavedProject]
    - return all users who saved this project

  _isSaved(userId: String, projectId: String) -> Boolean
    - check if user has saved a specific project

  _getCountByUser(userId: String) -> Number
    - return count of projects saved by user

  _getCountByProject(projectId: String) -> Number
    - return count of users who saved this project

operational principle
  Learners can bookmark projects they're interested in for later viewing. After save(userId: "learner1", projectId: "proj123"), then _isSaved(userId: "learner1", projectId: "proj123") returns true, and _getByUser(userId: "learner1") includes this project.

</concept_spec>
